                <pb facs="0781" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/755: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ireland</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-12T18:00:00-04:00">November 12, 1942—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>141. Your 204, October 16, and 210, October 25. Ambassador Winant has recently
                    telegraphed certain views on this subject. In a telegram today we are outlining
                    to him a proposed approach to be made by you and suggesting that you and he
                    discuss this approach during your forthcoming visit to London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
